    "closure": "complete outside-loop q deletion of both aligned common families",
    "statement": "The five common rows determine F(W)=b/W and A_1 proportional to (W-c)(W-i) in aligned family A, and F(W)=bW with A_1 proportional to (W+b)(W-i) in family B. The common loop uses the first root. Every product-level S1 or S2 survivor has one outside loop, whose zero q value and nonzero B_2 force the second root W=i. Its product F(i)=r in A or ib in B contradicts respectively the routed S1 quartic or S2 forced-loop product. Thus all aligned product survivors are empty before the other outside q rows or full interpolation.",
